pvals_main_man <- c(
  ".679",   # Lesion response: SOC vs NTAP, abstract/Results
  ".690",   # Lesion-level resolution score, Fig 1A/Results
  ".028"    # Within-patient average resolution, Results
)

# In the complete per-article file, every p-value appears in source order,
# with comments indicating table/figure, outcome, test and source when possible.
# The same format is used for the supplemental vector.

jaad_qc_article <- tibble::tibble(
  article_id = "0190962224027488",
  pvals_main_man = list(pvals_main_man),
  # ... existing QC fields and new explicitly named fields ...
  pvalue_qc_status_man = "legacy_verified",
  new_fields_review_status_man = "pending"
)
```

The snippet is explanatory only; the complete generated `.R` file, prompt, and template contain all required fields. **Do not paste this abbreviated example over an article annotation.** For articles with extensive supplements, use headings by supplemental table, outcome, and analysis, and preferably inline `#` result labels beside values. Maintain original ordering and the distinction between p-value operators (`=`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`) and numeric thresholds. The raw machine JSON retains the occurrence-level context even when the human-facing vector is compact.

