**Research aim clarified.** The Open Inference Project investigates statistical information published in articles, not relative performance of successive LLM generations. The model is an extraction instrument. Keep original article materials and stage outputs immutable; the field-level canonical article record is the best-supported research datum, with human correction when performed. Do not regenerate already adjudicated counts when GPT models or prompts change. New variables can be populated incrementally; altered definitions require deliberate migration. Freeze a dated research snapshot at manuscript analysis.

