Read the frozen Stage 05 records as INPUTS; do NOT redo extraction in this stage. First reconcile inside each table, endpoint, model and population block; then cross-block and cross-source. Assign canonical R00001... only when outcome, contrast/predictor, cohort, analytic method, model, adjustment and source evidence support the proposed equivalence. A report appearing in figure, text, and table may be one R; distinct Cox coefficient rows are separate R even if all report p<0.001. Do not silently merge dissimilar timepoint, adjusted/unadjusted, matched/unmatched, subgroups, or operationalizations. Track confidence and explicit reasons. For EACH P ID output occurrence_to_result.json with exactly one row containing occurrence_id, result_id or null, disposition (new_test/repeated_report/unresolved), reason, evidence, confidence. Every P ID must be mapped or explicitly unresolved. Generate canonical results Table A named `reconciled_results` with result_id,p,group,source,role,result and Table B named `analysis_groups` with group,outcome,role,structure,adjustment_context. Provide sources of R↔P crosslinks and partial coverage. For uncertain survival summaries (median vs landmark rates), never blanket-merge based solely on repeated p expression.

