Match HTML/PDF MAIN table records by table ID + normalized row hierarchy + column context + p operator/value. Report matched rows, HTML-only, PDF-only, value disagreements, label disagreements, and uncertain matches. Compare both counts PER table and row-level values. Save source_reconciliation/main_html_pdf_comparison.json plus discrepancy ledger listing raw evidence and source locators. Resolve by examining original PDF page/figure and, where appropriate, HTML table; confidence and reason must be explicit. If inaccessible, leave unresolved; do not promote source completeness. Once resolved, create one canonical main-table occurrence per PRINTED CELL (not per format); separately account for abstract/narrative/figure reports. If only one main format exists, state single-source confidence and do not pretend a dual-format comparison was performed.

STAGE 04 — SUPPLEMENT INVENTORY AND EXTRACTION
For each numbered supplement/table separately, prefer source-native DOCX structured tables when provided; independently compare with PDF if both representations exist, deduplicating logical cells. For PDF-only supplements use page-image/table-aware reading with explicit column and section context. Extract each p-value plus row name, parent covariate (for indented factor levels), outcome, risk set/cohort, adjustment, model family, reference group, estimate/CI if printed, page/table/cell. Preserve operator and source order. Note empty/no-p-value tables explicitly. For very long Cox tables process in bounded blocks per outcome/model with completeness counts and carry state between blocks. Don't conflate different coefficient tests with an omnibus category p-value. BEFORE extracting p cells, enumerate all explicit subsection headers, page-break continuations, populations, model types, table titles and transition row boundaries into a SOURCE BLOCK REGISTRY; review PDF page images whenever an endpoint heading sits near a page break. Assign block IDs and paragraph/row spans, freeze the registry as source_reconciliation/source_blocks.json, and extract against that registry rather than carrying forward the most recently seen endpoint. On transition, reset endpoint/population/model and parent-predictor context; never silently inherit the previous block into a new numbered table. For descriptive cohort tables, endpoint is `descriptive_characteristics` (not the survival endpoint of the previous table). If a PDF heading is missing or ambiguous, set outcome to unknown and flag unanchored/partial; do not guess based on neighboring coefficients.


STAGE 04B — MANDATORY BLOCK-HEADER CHECKPOINT (BEFORE ANY LABELED OCCURRENCE)
The source_block_registry is scientific evidence, not a post-hoc field generated from already-assigned P labels. For each numbered table, partition every numbered section according to literal heading and page/row boundaries. Include table ID; block ID; printed heading; normalized endpoint (or descriptive_characteristics); cohort/analysis unit; stage of disease; treatment restriction; adjustment; model family; source locator; start/end positions; heading confidence; and how continuations were recognized. Each p cell must belong to exactly ONE block. Every block must have a documented source heading or a documented continuation link to an earlier heading. Force a semantic-reset when transitioning table IDs even if the next table has no statistical endpoint. Audit the first, last and page-break-adjacent rows of EVERY block; flags become unresolved rather than inheriting the preceding endpoint.

