REVIEWER CLASSIFICATION RULES
- Boolean TRUE=source-positive; FALSE=source-negative after adequate inspection; NA=not sufficiently assessed. Never infer an affirmative from model convention alone.
- P values are printed character strings retaining <, >, = operators; do not silently turn <0.001 into exact 0.001.
- Reconciled results count is number of unique supported tests, NOT number of printed rows, outcome families, timepoints, covariate values, or model configurations.
- "Significant" means under the source-defined threshold and applicable adjustment; nominal significance is distinct. If threshold/adjustment not knowable mark unknown.
- Explicitly flag conflicts between source formats, between narrative and table, and within supplements (e.g. nearby survival summaries displaying different p-values) without resolving by guess.
- No results or methods from unrelated articles may be imported or used as defaults. Never refer to any demonstration article as required context.

