OPEN INFERENCE — SCIENTIFIC QUESTION LINKAGE v1.15.2 (ACTIVE; ADDITIVE)

Perform after P/R/G reconciliation and the article-level evidence and operational outcomes inventory. Do not alter P, R, G, existing 111 fields, or verification flags. Identify a SMALL number of source-supported research questions (typically 1–8). Questions are clinical/scientific propositions, NOT individual coefficient rows, individual p-values, different Cox adjustments, or generic model-family headings. If authors do not explicitly enumerate questions, mark `author_status=inferred` and use a paraphrase and source. Do not fabricate quotations or presume that a question is prespecified. Descriptive questions may be included but labeled `question_type=descriptive`. A propensity-matched analysis generally links to its existing scientific question as `robustness`, not a new question. Cohorts and endpoints must not be conflated.

REQUIRED R TABLES after `operational_outcomes` and BEFORE `jaad_qc_article`:
`scientific_questions <- tibble::tribble(~question_id,~question_text,~question_type,~author_status,~source_locator,~source_evidence,~interpretive_caveat, ...)`
`question_group_links <- tibble::tribble(~question_id,~group_id,~outcome_id,~link_role,~link_rationale, ...)`
