<summary><span class="oi-callout-title">Pilot B · Li et al. — 50-page supplement and high-density statistical reporting</span></summary>
<div class="oi-callout-body">

**Latest run report (approximately 18 min 33 sec):** **1,047** proposed canonical printed P occurrences; **994** proposed distinct statistical R results; **3** explicit unresolved P-to-R identities; **50** accepted repeat links. Main **HTML 63** accepted observations (35 table cells + 28 prose), main **PDF 71** accepted observations (35 table cells + 36 prose/caption), and supplemental **PDF 976** accepted values over eight tables/50 pages. The two main-article formats are *alternative representations of the same publication*, so their observations are **not simply added**. The earlier intermediate extraction had **1,044 P / 992 R** because three p-value-column **`1.00`** entries were omitted; the latest report identifies all three and passes the targeted validator sentinel.

The output reports **1,047/1,047 accepted PDF occurrences** with native coordinates (71 main + 976 supplement); two excluded Methods significance/selection thresholds retain separate candidate-coordinate records. The **23-table schema**, **six paired QC modules**, source provenance and unresolved/decision ledgers were generated, and the deterministic reconciliation validator reported **PASS**. The output itself remains **PARTIAL** because machine consistency is not a proof of semantic identity or exhaustive scientific correctness. Native Rscript syntax/execution and human-edit export validation are explicitly **NOT_RUN**.

Specific cases retained for review include Table I mean versus median follow-up (**p = .04** in each location); targeted-therapy OS (**p = .21** for median OS versus **p = .24** for the five-year/figure report); ICI MSS (**HR 0.56, p = .001** versus adjusted **HR 0.54, p < .001**); and LRC (**p < .001** in abstract versus **p = .001** in adjusted supplement with HR 1.17). These are scientifically meaningful candidates for source adjudication, **not automatically corrected errors**.

</div>
