- If a display cannot be resolved, leave the section pending and record an
  unresolved case rather than changing to an invented count.
- Canonical distinct result count = number of DISTINCT non-null, reconciled R IDs
  containing a reported p-value, not number of occurrences and not count of rows
  if there are uncertain classifications. Printed-occurrence count = canonical P
  IDs (including repeats), not combined HTML+PDF counts. Report both along with
  unresolved P/R cases; do not assert final count from an unverified proposal.
- The R script is the single HUMAN EDIT surface. Machine originals and full
  P/R/schema JSON remain frozen as model proposals. An assembly step reads the
  six review scripts, joins edits by canonical article/R/P IDs into a SEPARATE
  derived `human_reviewed_data/` export and revalidates IDs, cardinalities,
  literal p values, source locators, non-matching reports, unresolved flags and
  field-ownership rules. NEVER silently overwrite frozen original proposals.
- A previously confirmed display changed afterward must be marked STALE until
  reconfirmed. Retain the original vs changed value and the relevant section ID.
  If native R/assembler or fingerprint testing is unavailable, report NOT RUN;
  comments alone do not constitute verified scientific database integration.
- Module 02 has separate one-comment confirmations for design/framework,
  registration (especially timing), primary outcome, multiplicity and CI reporting.
  Do not force completion of module 03 power/effect size/AI to complete module 02.
- No review of SHA-256 values, file hashes or schema-internal columns is required
  for manuscript scientific QC. Hashes, source-inventory equivalences and key/FK
  structural checks are MACHINE gates, never human science confirmations.

SIX-FILE RSTYLE AND NAVIGATION ACCEPTANCE
- Each `.R` file is independently parseable and sourceable; no human file needs
  to `source()` another scientific review module, and files should begin with an
  independently functioning `qc_confirm` implementation or equivalent status
  collection. Mark all sections commented and pending initially.
- Use native RStudio headings ending `----`, stable labels, clear horizontal
  separators, one scientific object per QC unit and short comments.
- Avoid `article_data.R`, QMD, HTML preview, giant column-wise vectors, nested
  verbose per-P lists in results QC, and model vs human filename mismatches.
- Put minimal computer-check summaries in reports, not in manually verified
  scientific R sections. A source block which lacks source provenance must be
  `PENDING`, not guessed.
- Frozen six scripts and initial human six scripts must be byte-identical. No
  script starts with live confirmations. The initial run may be `PARTIAL` if
  source coverage, reconciliation or native execution is incomplete.

CURRENT-ARTICLE ACCEPTANCE CHECKS — APPLY ONLY TO THE UPLOADED ARTICLE
These checks assess THIS extraction, not historical examples or overall software readiness.
No unrelated articles or pilot datasets are required or expected.
1. Verify six matching, initially unconfirmed R review modules in both directories;
   keep Module 01 display-first in the uploaded publication's table/figure order,
   then narrative-only results. Keep unrelated scientific domains out of Module 01.
   Verify one provenance-derived primary source-location comment immediately before
   EVERY distinct-R/unresolved-P review row, and concise source-status comments for
   inspected display regions without separate numerical p values. Confirm primary
   comments against the frozen P locator; DO NOT populate repeat-location cells
   with the primary source location.
2. Execute the MANDATORY SOURCE-COVERAGE GATE above first: independently
   enumerate main HTML vs PDF and all actual supplement formats, including EACH
   page's first and last p-value cells, every numbered main table, abstract,
   narrative and figure/caption. Validate source-observation dispositions by
   physical page and logical block. Mark uninspected or unreconciled coverage
   PARTIAL or NOT_RUN. Identical HTML/PDF depictions are one canonical P.
3. Execute the MANDATORY STATISTICAL-IDENTITY RECONCILIATION GATE above as a
   separate step AFTER freezing P. Check its per-P decision ledger and plausible
   candidate pairs, including within-analysis and across narrative/figure/table
   searches. Do not accept one-R-per-P default assignments without evidence of
   candidate search. Then cross-check the complete canonical P inventory against
   all Module 01 `p_ids`: each P appears exactly once across review rows.
   For each R row, secondary P IDs must match the named entries and locators in
   `other_printings` and `other_locations`. Each confidently reconciled R belongs
   to exactly one primary review row; ambiguous P-to-R cases remain unresolved.
4. Validate table ownership and correction/export consistency across all six
   modules, the frozen 23-table originals, P/R identifiers, values and provenance.
   In Module 03, assert ALL 12 `articles` and ALL 9 `article_authorship`
   fields are visible and editable in the two FIRST, distinct R sections,
   each with a separate pending `qc_confirm` marker; both must match their
   canonical `article_id`. Test human-edit to separate reviewed-export mapping
   if a working assembler exists, otherwise report NOT_RUN.
   Verify Module 02 distinguishes explicit author "nominal" wording from
   adjustment interpretation, procedure reporting, method and family, with
   source-specific evidence; do not infer unadjusted from nonreporting.
   Verify that confirmations remain independent and all begin pending.
5. Test R parsing/source execution and section-change fingerprints only when
   available. Report PASSED solely for checks actually executed; otherwise NOT_RUN.
   Never infer scientific verification from structural success.
6. If any required source, identity or structural check fails or cannot run,
   provide an explicit PARTIAL output and issue ledger, not a fabricated PASS.

FIRST MANUSCRIPT COMPLETION RULE
Only Modules 01 and 02 can gate publication-one reviewer completion. Each module
is independently confirmable with source-level status and exception ledger; a
paper can legitimately be publication-one eligible while Modules 03–06 remain
unreviewed. Do not call an article or later domains entirely human verified.
In advance define essential methods variables for that manuscript; do not
silently make first-paper QC require Module 03 bibliographic/authorship
verification, sample-size/power, detailed effect estimates, AI, Q/O/G,
models/DAG or claims. Bibliographic metadata and author identities are still
extracted and retained for manuscript identification and downstream joins; only
their separate HUMAN confirmation is deferred by default.

