APPENDIX — COMPLETE HUMAN-READABLE FIELD REFERENCE (SCIENTIFIC SCHEMA 3.0)
=======================================================================
Purpose: Let a reviewer inspect every field expected from Open Inference without
having to read the machine-readable JSON schema. The schema and dictionary above
remain authoritative; these short explanations are a human-reading aid, not a
second extraction contract. Names and table order are generated from the schema.

This appendix inventories 269 COLUMN DEFINITIONS in 23 tables across seven domains.
A field is a column within its table. The same name in different tables denotes
a distinct table-specific column; IDs, metadata and evidence fields count too.
These are not 269 independent variables observed once per article. Individual
papers produce different numbers of result, model, term and occurrence records.
Null/unresolved values are expected when source evidence is insufficient.

DOMAIN 1 — ARTICLE AND STUDY
---------------------------
TABLE: articles  (12 fields; one per article)
001. article_id — Stable article identifier used to join all scientific records; use a publisher PII when available.
002. title_short — Short descriptive title of this article
003. journal — Journal title as published
004. publication_year — Year of publication shown in the article citation.
005. publication_volume — Published volume
006. publication_issue — Published issue
007. publication_pages — Published page range or electronic article location.
008. doi — Article DOI
009. online_publication_date — Online publication date, ISO format if known
010. article_type — Article type exactly as published
011. article_type_standardized — Controlled research/article type
012. is_research — Whether original primary research eligible for cohort

TABLE: article_authorship  (9 fields; one per article)
013. article_id — Article identifier linking author identities and affiliations to the publication.
014. first_author_name — First author exactly as printed in the article byline.
015. first_author_affiliations — Published institutional affiliation(s) of first author
016. last_author_name — Last listed author; this does not automatically identify the senior author.
017. last_author_affiliations — Published affiliation(s) of last author
