For EVERY R-centered row (and every unresolved P row), insert ONE short R comment
immediately BEFORE the row in the corresponding `tribble()`; a comment is legal
R syntax and does NOT add a `tribble` field or change the six mandatory columns.
Derive the comment deterministically from the FROZEN primary P record and its
linked source observation/provenance; DO NOT reconstruct it from memory, copy
secondary locations, or guess physical page/journal pagination. Format:

    # R00012 / P00004 — Main PDF physical p4; journal p49; Results narrative
    # R00013 / P00005 — Main PDF physical p4; journal p49; Results narrative

Each comment identifies the canonical R ID (or `R unresolved`), PRIMARY P ID,
source document (main manuscript vs named supplement; HTML if no PDF), physical
PDF page when there is a PDF, printed journal page ONLY when printed/confirmed,
and source category + named location (abstract, Results narrative, main table,
figure/caption, supplemental table/figure). These examples are not source facts
for the article being processed. If a particular locator is unknown, state
`journal page unavailable` / `physical PDF page unavailable` rather than inventing
one. A P with only one printing STILL receives its primary comment, while its
`other_printings` and `other_locations` remain `list(character(0))`.

These comments are NONAUTHORITATIVE NAVIGATION AIDS, not human-confirmation
markers and not a second editable scientific source. The P coordinates, full
source locator and source hashes remain in frozen provenance and data JSON.
Changes made by a reviewer to a comment do not silently change the backend;
record a provenance correction for separate review/export. Validate that every
Module 01 primary comment's R/P IDs and recorded primary source location agree
