### Scientific schema and stage ownership {.unlisted}

The verified v1.19.0 reference application bundles **schema 3.1.0 (25 scientific tables and 302 table-qualified columns)** and shared dictionary **3.1.1-draft.4**. The underlying two-stage program remains organized by scientific dependencies, not model capability.

| Scientific operation | Editable R modules | Role |
|:--|:--|:--|
| **Stage I** | **01** article/study; **02** inferential methods/planning; **03** physical P observations, proposed distinct R identities and P→R reconciliation | Originally owns **150** canonical fields; source inventory and stable P/R foundation |
| **Stage II** | **04** outcomes/models; **05** scientific questions and R→Q; **06** claims, evidence links and inferential footprint | Owns the remaining **152** canonical fields; inherits Stage I identities and proposes corrections separately |

The distinction is mandatory: **P** is a logical printed p-value appearance across equivalent renderings of a published source; **R** is a distinct source-identifiable statistical result. Printed appearances are frozen evidence; matching numerical values do not establish common R identity. R may have multiple P, one P or no P (for example, a Bayesian posterior summary). P, R, tests, hypotheses, scientific questions and inferential families are **not synonymous**.

### Scientific authority and verification {.unlisted}

The six editable R QC scripts are the scientific authority. Untouched model originals belong in `qc/model_unverified/`; human working copies belong in `qc/human_verified/`. Reviewers attest specific source-reviewed QC scopes through **actual `qc_confirm()` calls**. Placement inside a folder named `Verified/` is not, by itself, human approval. Model-proposed, machine-validated and human-verified statuses remain separate.

Stage II selects a complete Stage I package by its internal Modules 01–03; multiple candidates require explicit selection. Its `human_reviewed` mode requires current native R scope approvals and the exact Stage I dictionary pin. `machine_continuation` explicitly permits still-pending Stage I scientific inputs and makes **no approval claim**. The package includes an exact-byte Stage I snapshot and reports missing evidence artifacts as transport gaps. All retained human decisions and source inventories must survive handoff.

**Model-reasoning-aware architecture remains a hypothesis.** Lower-complexity descriptive tasks and higher-complexity P→R or R→Q/C reasoning can eventually be routed differently, with targeted escalation; no five-tier router was adopted. For Paper 1, a **single substantive higher-reasoning Stage I model pass** plus deterministic inventory and human QC is a plausible, not yet scientifically proven, default.

