OPEN INFERENCE 3.1 — STAGE 1 OF 2: ARTICLE FACTS, METHODS, AND FROZEN STATISTICAL RESULTS
Article-level R-first extraction contract · 2026-10-17

SCOPE
Read the attached sanitized OIP_SOURCE_MANIFEST.json first to establish the exact article ID and source file hashes. Process every main-article source format actually supplied (HTML, PDF, or both), plus every supplied supplement, figure, caption, table and Methods section. Do not treat an absent source format as a missing document or a zero-result inspection. Use the attached OIP31_RUNTIME.zip for the exact OIP schema 3.1, dictionary, validation scripts, source-freeze contract, and R QC conventions. Ignore old all-in-one START_HERE contracts if found inside the runtime or historical documents. Stage 1 generates ONLY three reviewable R QC modules, plus machine evidence/validation files needed to substantiate them. Do NOT generate Modules 04–06, scientific claim→R links, operational question prose for every R, or the completed 25-table schema package.

MODULES (NEW TWO-STAGE ORDER; separate from legacy 3.1 module numbering)
01_article_study_design_qc.R — bibliographic identity, authors, DOI, volume/issue, design, populations, endpoints, sample size, registration/protocol/analysis plan evidence, prespecified versus post hoc classification only where evidenced. Every material classification has verbatim source evidence/locator and review status. Unreported != absent. Include an author-stated aim/major-claim source index if inexpensive, but defer claim validity and R links.
02_inferential_methods_qc.R — statistical framework (frequentist/Bayesian/mixed/unclear), declared methods, tests, inference thresholds, statistical planning, reported multiplicity strategy, model families, analyses named in Methods, any author-supplied DAG or rationale for covariates. NO coefficient-by-coefficient reconstructive modeling. Preserve uncertainty/source quotes; distinguish covariate adjustment from multiple-testing adjustment.
03_results_p_to_r_qc.R — exhaustive printed P inventory + proposed P→R statistical identity and table-by-table R results, with labels, exact printed literals, coordinates and source excerpts. Inventory every printed P from the supplied source set, including main prose, tables, figure annotations, captions, and supplements. Measure physical PDF coordinates for all PDF-derived observations; use DOM/section/row locators for HTML-only evidence. Reconcile duplicated HTML/PDF representations ONLY when both main formats are present. Never infer equivalence by p-value numerical equality alone. A distinct R may be linked to multiple P; do not force sequential R numbers to be contiguous. Respect any supplied, explicitly approved previous identity decisions.

CONDITIONAL SOURCE-FORMAT COVERAGE — MANDATORY
Read the manifest first and record which original main formats were actually supplied. Do NOT require both formats:
- BOTH HTML and PDF supplied: Pass A and independent Pass B each inspect both formats (and every supplement/figure). Reconcile A versus B within each source, then reconcile equivalent main HTML/PDF depictions using original table/row/contrast evidence. Preserve both source observations and one canonical P when they are the same printing across formats; flag discrepancies instead of choosing silently.
- PDF ONLY: complete two genuinely independent PDF-based source scans (e.g., native word/geometry and a separate layout/table-aware reading), including every PDF table continuation, narrative and available figures/supplements. Reconcile Pass A with Pass B and freeze canonical P. Cross-format HTML/PDF comparison is NOT APPLICABLE, not FAILED, and no HTML observations or phantom HTML zero-regions may be invented.
- HTML ONLY: complete two independent HTML-based source scans (e.g., DOM/table-node traversal and independent structured-text/section traversal), including any supplied supplements/figures. Reconcile A with B; record stable HTML DOM/table/row/source locators, not fabricated PDF pages, PDF coordinates or PDF observations. Cross-format comparison is NOT APPLICABLE, not FAILED.
- PDF main with HTML supplements (or HTML main with PDF supplements): inspect every format actually present, but compare equivalent presentations ONLY when the same work/result is reported in multiple supplied sources; do not assume supplements are alternate representations of the main article.
- Only a missing main article in ALL supported forms blocks extraction; an absent individual format does not. If a supplied source is corrupt or unreadable, mark its coverage INCOMPLETE/FAIL rather than pretending it was never supplied.
In the Stage 1 report give `source_format_mode` (html_pdf/pdf_only/html_only), source inventory and hashes, two-pass reconciliation status, cross-format status (performed or NOT_APPLICABLE), PDF coordinate coverage denominator (zero/N/A if no PDF observations), and any source-specific exceptions. Do not carry Li-specific expected HTML/PDF counts into other articles. Both independent passes remain mandatory with one source format.

SOURCE FREEZE IS A GATE
Implement the companion runtime's double independent source scan A and B over EVERY ACTUALLY SUPPLIED source, inspected-zero regions, physical PDF coordinates wherever a PDF is supplied, source reconciliation, frozen canonical P ledger, source hashes, and VALIDATE_SOURCE_FREEZE.py gate exactly as documented there. Preserve stage-specific files in source_reconciliation/ and validation/. Do not abbreviate supplement inspections to save runtime. If genuinely unfinished, return honest PARTIAL outputs and precise resume information; never produce a synthetic PASS. R identities remain proposed pending independent QC. Distinguish P (printed occurrences) from R (statistical tests) rigorously.

HUMAN QC INTERFACE
Readable tibble::tribble blocks organized by article section / source table. Each scope has its actual editable data and a commented # qc_confirm("...") as in OIP's QC modules. Include explanatory comments and source locators. Never pre-uncomment confirmation or claim user approval. Name files ARTICLEID_01_article_study_design_qc.R, ARTICLEID_02_inferential_methods_qc.R, ARTICLEID_03_results_p_to_r_qc.R, where ARTICLEID is the exact article_id from the source manifest (e.g., S0190962224027683). Output a ZIP containing exactly those three .R scripts, source evidence/ledgers, validation reports, and a concise README. Avoid generic filler; mark uncertainties explicitly. Actual tool execution status (Python and R separately) must be reported. NO simulated attestation.

FINAL P→R IDENTITY CROSS-CHECK (AFTER THE P INVENTORY IS FROZEN)
For each source table, compare each statistical result with potentially repeated abstract, narrative, caption, main-table, and supplemental printings. Do not treat matching P numerals as proof of a shared test, but do not assume different source locations imply different tests. Give special attention to repeated endpoint/contrast/model/effect reports, and adjacent alternative descriptive summaries (e.g. median and mean follow-up). Preserve proposed distinct tests wherever identity genuinely differs; leave uncertainty visible when evidence cannot resolve it. This cross-check changes only provisional R mapping, NEVER the frozen P observations. If supplied prior human-reviewed R decisions, preserve them or flag explicit conflicts. Report how many source P printings map to each R, and highlight plausible unmerged repeats for human QC.

