### Decision: constrain the measurement problem

**Working manuscript:** *Statistical Inference and Reporting Practices in Published Clinical Research* (Paper 1). The project moved from the broad 302-column OIP canonical scientific schema toward a **short, inspectable Paper 1 measurement instrument**. The master codebook is deliberately parked as a reference—not deleted and not made a routine human-QC burden.

The consolidated **Paper 1 investigator-review codebook now has 53 table-qualified definitions**: **17 article-level scientific measures** and **36 supporting identity, evidence, repeating-statement and P/R fields**. This is a **proposed review contract**, distinct from the currently installed v1.19.1 `active_paper1` extraction profile; these counts do not mean 53 new human-QC judgments per article.

| Paper 1 measure family | What is intentionally included | Boundary |
|:--|:--|:--|
| Study design and size | Assigned intervention versus observational; prospective versus retrospective; randomization; primary-analysis N and counted unit | These design dimensions must not be collapsed into one mutually exclusive class; lesions ≠ people |
| Scientific reporting | Frequentist, Bayesian or mixed reporting; registration and timing; protocol/SAP availability; primary outcome and analysis prespecification | Authors’ reports ≠ verified prior practice; no routine external registry lookup in Stage I |
| Inference reporting | Stated alpha threshold; multiplicity as multiple scoped author statements; reported covariate adjustment | Unmentioned adjustment ≠ explicit no adjustment; multiplicity control ≠ covariate adjustment |
| P/R accounting | Every distinct printed p-value occurrence (P) and every distinct source-identifiable statistical result (R) | R is not independent hypotheses; missing source coverage limits count claims |

No full model ontology, hypothesis reconstruction, causal/DAG analysis, or claims mapping was activated for Paper 1; these remain potential Stage II / later-paper scientific work.

