| **03 · P-to-R reconciliation** | Horizontal **seven-column** `tribble()` with one visual result per row and compact multiline cells | Human/model-assisted QC of P capture, source placement, result identity, and reconciliation |

**Approved seven-column ordering for Script 03:** `RID` · `PID` · `Source` · `p-value` · `Effect / CI` · `Result label` · `Identity / Test`. In the review source, short IDs remain narrow; long labels and test identities wrap. **PID and Source are adjacent**, and for one RID with multiple PIDs the corresponding PIDs, source locators, and exact p-value strings are **line-aligned** (for example, `P00031 → Results ¶3`; `P00094 → Supplemental Table 3`). The `Source` column is a short, human-readable free-text locator; granular PDF coordinates and source representation IDs remain in provenance records.

A distinct R **may have no printed P**, for example an interval estimate. An observed P whose R assignment cannot be established **must remain unresolved**, not receive an invented RID. Underlying P occurrence, R identity, and P→R relationship ledgers remain normalized: a grouped visual row is not permission to merge records or erase separate provenance.

### Multiplicity remains explicitly verified in Script 02

The article-level summary is insufficient on its own. A separate repeatable multiplicity section captures **each reported method or nonadjustment statement**, verbatim method, affected scope (or `unclear`), stated error criterion (FWER/FDR only when explicit), and supporting source text. Multiple methods can coexist. This section receives its own human confirmation and is **not** deferred to an unreviewed backend field.

