For Stage II’s inferential footprint, **Stage I must verify distinct result identity**. A trustworthy `Result label` plus `Identity / Test` distinguishes analyses that differ by comparison, population, time point, subgroup, or adjusted/unadjusted method when reported. There is no Stage I requirement to reconstruct every fitted model, assumption, covariate or test family. Stage II may retrieve additional methods from the primary source, but those are **new Stage II proposals requiring new QC**, not automatically inherited truth.

**Independent coverage gate:** source manifests, equivalent HTML/PDF reconciliation, physical P inventory, inspected regions and missing-supplement status must still be checked separately from visual R-row approval. P totals cannot be declared complete if relevant source coverage is incomplete. A machine PASS is not human scientific verification.

