<div class="oi-callout-body">

**Scientific objective.** Pilot a comprehensive Stage I extraction that counts printed p-value occurrences (**PPOs**), printed inferential occurrences (**PIOs**), distinct inferential results (**DIRs**) and the P-associated subset (**DPRs**) in **Wang, Walker, and Li**. Earlier drafts deferred non-P inference to Stage II; on October 20 we elected to test capturing the full evidence inventory once and verifying it in coherent source-based blocks, then reserve model reconstruction, scientific questions and explicit author claims for Stage II.

**Counting rules discussed and selected for pilot:**

| Unit | Working scientific counting rule | Key / derivation |
|:--|:--|:--|
| PPO | One numeric printed p-value expression per logical publication location. Equivalent HTML/PDF renditions do not multiply occurrences; distinct printings do. | `ppo_id`; PID in review |
| PIO | One source-local reporting instance of an identifiable inferential target; compatible HR, CI, and p-value in the same reported finding form one PIO. | `pio_id` |
| DIR | One distinct source-supported statistical inference, not each of its printed statistical components or every repeated appearance. | `dir_id`; RID in review |
| DPR | Distinct DIR associated with at least one mapped, accepted printed p-value occurrence. | Derived subset of DIR; not another result-ID system |

**Scientific identity examples.** A hazard ratio, its confidence interval and its p-value generally describe **one DIR**, not three. One global log-rank comparison is one test-DIR; arm-specific Kaplan–Meier landmark probabilities with separately reported inferential intervals count as distinct estimate-DIR candidates. An unadjusted and an adjusted Cox coefficient generally represent distinct results. Repeated publication of the same analysis increases occurrence counts but not the DIR count. A covariate merely included for adjustment does not create an extra DIR, whereas a reported inferential coefficient for that covariate can. Unidentifiable inferential-looking material stays in an unresolved candidate ledger, not a fabricated DIR.

**Stage boundary.** Stage I describes and source-verifies **reported evidence and lightweight analysis context**. Stage II will relate inherited DIR identities to **outcomes, scientific/operational questions, explicit claims, and SPEC/FIT model reconstructions**. A model group is not a confirmed fitted instance. Stage II must not silently reassign human-verified Stage I identities.

**Status as of October 20:** scientifically explicit **pilot rules**, not established validity across the Wang, Walker, Li corpus. No real-paper extraction or human QC is claimed.

