<div class="oi-day-body">

<details class="oi-callout oi-log-entry oi-milestone" open>
<summary><span class="oi-callout-title">Stage II scientific architecture and integrated two-stage workflow</span><span class="oi-badge">DAY MILESTONE</span></summary>
<div class="oi-callout-body">

**October 21 advance.** Two linked developments turned the October 20 comprehensive Stage I design into a versioned *two-stage* research pilot: (1) a first, inspectable **Stage II-only data dictionary** and source-grounded instructions; and (2) a Shiny handoff path that selects the **actual reviewed Stage I R files** from one article-level parent folder, rather than requiring manually assembled uploads or reconstituting the science from the original extraction JSON. A subsequent v1.19.4 refinement made the human QC steps practical table by table, including publication metadata.

| Deliverable | Version / scientific state at end of day | Boundary |
|:--|:--|:--|
| Stage I scientific data | **99 fields / 12 tables**, October 20 unique-field naming ontology Draft 3 retained | Still requires source-based article QC; no change to counting rules today |
| Stage II scientific data | **128 proposed fields / 16 tables**, Stage II Draft 1 (96 core, 32 extensions) | Research design and codebook, **not** investigator-verified scientific results |
| Application and instructions | **OIP 3.1 Shiny v1.19.4**, Stage I Draft 5 instructions, Stage II Draft 1 instructions | Versioned *pilot*: mechanical tests and Mac launch observed; full native R/QC/real article Stage II validation remains pending |

**Research principle:** Stage I reports source-grounded evidence; Stage II extends verified Stage I identities into outcomes, model structures, stated questions, operational targets, and published claims. A printed p-value, reported result, fitted instance, scientific question, and author claim are **not the same scientific unit**. One may connect to many of another, or to none when source evidence does not support a link.

</div>
</details>

<details class="oi-callout oi-log-entry oi-consolidation">
<summary><span class="oi-callout-title">Stage II Draft 1 · 128-field scientific data dictionary and handoff schematic</span><span class="oi-badge">DATA DICTIONARY</span></summary>
<div class="oi-callout-body">

### Separate Stage II dictionary; preserve Stage I as the verified foundation

The earlier OIP 3.1 reference contained **302 historical fields**, **152 owned by Stage II**. Rather than wholesale promotion, the October 21 draft defines **128 new Stage II-only variables** in **16 scientific tables**, with **no field-name collisions** against the 99-field Stage I dictionary. The accompanying historical crosswalk accounts for all 152 former Stage II fields but **does not claim a lossless 152-to-128 conversion**. The readable four-column investigator codebook retains `variable / type / definition / options` and provides filters for core versus extension fields.

| Module | Tables / key concepts | Main scientific separation |
|:--|:--|:--|
| **04 · Outcomes and models** | Operational outcomes **O**, model **SPEC**, fitted instances **FIT**, reported model terms, model-building decisions, and DIR-to-FIT links. **58 fields**. | A model formula/specification can underlie several fits; a fit can produce several DIRs. A reported coefficient is not an entire fitted model. |
| **05 · Questions** | Explicit scientific questions **Q**, reconstructed operational inferential targets **OPQ**, DIR-to-question links and optional OPQ groupings. **31 fields**. | What authors *said they asked* is distinct from the operational question recoverable from an inferential result. |
| **06 · Claims and footprint** | Printed author claims **C**, claim-to-DIR and claim-to-Q links, optional claim assessments, inferential families and family-to-DIR links. **39 fields**. | Extract claims independently before assessing correspondence to evidence. A claim is not automatically a hypothesis test, and a DIR need not map to a claim. |

**Prefix–suffix convention.** Proposed names use stable entity-specific prefixes and consistent semantic suffixes, for example `spec_model_family`, `spec_source_locator`, `fit_spec_id`, `fit_source_locator`, `claim_id`, `claim_source_locator`. Stage I's `article_id`, `ppo_id`, `pio_id`, `dir_id` and `analysis_group_id` retain their existing scientific identities. Stage II foreign keys are explicit and article scoped; no second RID namespace is created. Mapping evidence and ambiguous or unsupported links must be kept, not guessed.

**Missing-value editorial clarification (proposed, not yet a dictionary revision).** The draft's shorthand *“source-faithful, typed missing”* means report only source-supported values and use a real type-appropriate `NA` when absent. The reason (not reported, unclear, not applicable, not assessed) should be separately represented where the schema supports it. This term was flagged for clearer wording in a future codebook revision; the Draft 1 options have **not** been silently changed.

